{"seq": 21, "t": 30.498, "type": "plan", "escalation": false, "diagnosis": "The upgrade to Pydantic v2 removed `ConstrainedInt` and `ConstrainedFloat` from `pydantic.types`, causing import errors that prevent test collection. Additionally, several APIs were renamed or changed behavior: `parse_obj` \u2192 `model_validate`, `@validator` \u2192 `@field_validator`, `parse_obj_as` \u2192 `TypeAdapter.validate_python`, `alias` argument removed from `Field`, `Union` short\u2011circuit behavior changed, custom `__init__` and `__eq__` require migration, and `TypeError` in validators now propagates instead of being wrapped.", "dependency_changes": [], "steps": [{"file": "blocklib/validation/constrained_types.py", "change": "Replace `ConstrainedInt` and `ConstrainedFloat` with `Annotated[int, Field(ge=0)]` and `Annotated[float, Field(ge=0, le=1)]` for `PositiveInt` and `UnitFloat`.", "rules": ["R50", "R58", "R138", "R139"], "why": "Constrained* classes removed in V2; Annotated with Field constraints is the replacement."}, {"file": "blocklib/validation/__init__.py", "change": "Replace `@validator('config', pre=True, always=True, each_item=False)` with `@field_validator('config')` and adjust signature; replace `BlockingSchemaModel.parse_obj(config)` with `BlockingSchemaModel.model_validate(config)`.", "rules": ["R37", "R39", "R119", "R120", "R339", "R9"], "why": "Validator decorator and parse_obj renamed; each_item/always=True removed in favor of Annotated types."}, {"file": "blocklib/pprllambdafold.py", "change": "Replace `LambdaConfig.parse_obj(config)` with `LambdaConfig.model_validate(config)`.", "rules": ["R9"], "why": "parse_obj renamed to model_validate in V2."}, {"file": "blocklib/pprlpsig.py", "change": "Replace `PSigConfig.parse_obj(config)` with `PSigConfig.model_validate(config)`.", "rules": ["R9"], "why": "parse_obj renamed to model_validate in V2."}, {"file": "blocklib/validation/lambda_fold_validation.py", "change": "Remove `alias` arguments from `Field` (e.g., `alias='bf-len'`) because V2 drops the alias parameter.", "rules": ["R20", "R13"], "why": "alias argument removed; V2 returns None for unset aliases."}, {"file": "blocklib/validation/psig_validation.py", "change": "Add `union_mode='left_to_right'` to the `feature: Union[int, str]` field to preserve V1 left\u2011to\u2011right matching.", "rules": ["R124"], "why": "V2 Union short\u2011circuits on first match; union_mode restores V1 behavior."}, {"file": "blocklib/validation/shared_blocking_config.py", "change": "Add `union_mode='left_to_right'` to `blocking_features: Union[List[int], List[str]]` field.", "rules": ["R124"], "why": "Same Union behavior change as above."}, {"file": "blocklib/pprlindex.py", "change": "Replace `parse_obj_as` with `TypeAdapter(...).validate_python(...)`; replace both custom `__init__` methods with `@root_validator`; adjust `__eq__` to compare model instances instead of dict.", "rules": ["R134", "R347", "R327", "R326"], "why": "parse_obj_as deprecated, custom __init__ not called, __eq__ no longer equals dict."}, {"file": "blocklib/candidate_blocks_generator.py", "change": "Replace custom `__init__` of `CandidateBlockingResult` with `@root_validator`.", "rules": ["R327"], "why": "Custom __init__ overrides are not called in V2; root_validator is the replacement."}, {"file": "blocklib/blocks_generator.py", "change": "In `check_block_object`, replace `raise TypeError(...)` with `raise ValidationError(...)` if this function is used as a validator; otherwise note that TypeError will propagate.", "rules": ["R41", "R122", "R345"], "why": "TypeError in validators no longer converted to ValidationError; must raise ValidationError explicitly."}], "risks": ["Union fields now short\u2011circuit on first match; `union_mode='left_to_right'` restores V1 behavior but must be verified.", "Alias argument removed from Field; any serialization/deserialization relying on aliases may break.", "TypeError raised in validators now propagates; `check_block_object` may need to raise ValidationError if used in validation context.", "Optional/nullable field logic now matches dataclasses; required/optional defaults may change subtly.", "Float-to-int conversion only allows zero decimal part; validation becomes stricter for numeric fields.", "__post_init__ now runs after validation; side\u2011effects in __post_init__ may occur at a different time.", "Regex engine switched to Rust crate; pattern matching behavior may differ for complex regexes."]}
